00:44:17,142 --> 00:44:23,142
Before the Flood is a 2016 documentary film about
climate change directed by Fisher Stevens.

11
00:48:42,857 --> 00:48:48,857
The film was produced as a collaboration between Stevens, Leonardo DiCaprio, James
Packer, Brett Ratner, Trevor Davidoski, and Jennifer Davisson Killoran.

12
00:53:08,571 --> 00:53:14,571
Martin Scorsese is an executive producer.

13
00:57:34,285 --> 00:57:40,285
The film covers effects of climate change in various regions of
the world, and discusses climate change denial.

14
01:02:00,000 --> 01:02:06,000
Numerous public figures are interviewed in the documentary.

15
01:06:25,714 --> 01:06:31,714
To offset the carbon emissions of the production, the
filmmakers paid a voluntary carbon tax.

16
01:10:51,428 --> 01:10:57,428
The soundtrack features compositions by Trent Reznor and
Atticus Ross, Mogwai and Gustavo Santaolalla.

17
01:15:17,142 --> 01:15:23,142
The film premiered at the Toronto International Film Festival in September 2016, and was released
theatrically on October 21, before airing on the National Geographic Channel on October 30.

18
01:19:42,857 --> 01:19:48,857
As part of National Geographic's commitment to covering climate change, the
documentary was made widely available and free of charge on various platforms.

19
01:24:08,571 --> 01:24:14,571
It received generally positive critical reviews.

20
01:28:34,285 --> 01:28:40,285
The film explores themes of society, climate change,
natural disaster, global warming, green energy.
